\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\b Galiluna Shield - End User License Agreement and Privacy Notice\b0\par
\fs20 Please read this before installing. By installing or using Galiluna Shield ("the Software") you agree to the terms below.\par
\b 1. What the Software does\b0\par
Galiluna Shield listens to the microphone and/or to the sound of selected programs on this computer, converts speech to text on this computer, compares the text against a list of red-flag words that you control, and saves alerts, transcripts, audio clips, recordings and reports to a folder on this computer.\par
\b 2. Privacy\b0\par
All speech recognition and analysis happen locally on this computer. The Software does not upload audio, transcripts, alerts or any personal data to the publisher or to anyone else. The only network access is a one-time download of the speech-recognition model on first run. Everything the Software produces is stored under the folder you choose (by default your Documents folder) and is under your control.\par
\b 3. Your responsibilities\b0\par
You are responsible for using the Software lawfully. Laws on recording conversations and monitoring minors differ by country and state; some require the consent of all parties. Use the Software only on computers you own or are authorised to monitor, and only to protect children in your care. Keep alerts, clips and recordings private and delete them when no longer needed.\par
\b 4. No guarantee of detection\b0\par
Speech recognition is imperfect. The Software may miss words, mishear words, or raise alerts for innocent speech. It is a tool to help a parent notice and investigate; it is not a substitute for supervision, conversation or professional help. Always listen to the audio clip before acting on an alert.\par
\b 5. License\b0\par
You are granted a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use the Software on computers in your household. You may not redistribute, resell or reverse-engineer the Software except where the law expressly permits it.\par
\b 6. Warranty and liability\b0\par
The Software is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the publisher is not liable for any damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Software, including missed detections or false alerts.\par
\b 7. Open-source components\b0\par
The Software includes whisper.cpp / Whisper.net (MIT license), NAudio (MIT license) and the .NET runtime (MIT license). Their license texts are included in the installation folder where required.\par
